ENTRY            23189   20250629   20260826   20260826       2323
SUBENT        23189001   20250629   20260826   20260826       2323
BIB                 10         56
TITLE      Determination of the 237Np(n,f) reaction cross section
            for En=4.5-5.3 MeV, using a MicroMegas
            detector assembly
AUTHOR     (M.Diakaki, M.Kokkoris, A.Kyrtsos, E.Skordis,
            C.T.Papadopoulos, R.Vlastou, A.Lagoyannis,
            S.Andriamonje)
INSTITUTE  (2GRCTUA,2GRCATH,2FR SAC)
REFERENCE  (J,EPJ/A,49,62,2013)
           #doi:10.1140/epja/i2013-13062-3
REL-REF    (N,,M.Diakaki,J,NDS,119,52,2014)
           Additional data point at En=5.56+/-0.08 MeV (not for
            addition in EXFOR)
FACILITY   (VDGT,2GRCATH) 5.5 MV HV TN-11 Tandem accelerator
INC-SOURCE (D-D) Deuterium gas target bombarded with deuteron
            beam at ~500 nA - 1 uA.
           --------------------------------------
             Ed       <Ed>         <En> (0-5deg)
             MeV       MeV            MeV
           --------------------------------------
             2.0  1.39 +/- 0.14  4.58 +/- 0.14
             2.2  1.63 +/- 0.13  4.85 +/- 0.13
             2.4  1.86 +/- 0.12  5.09 +/- 0.12
             2.6  2.08 +/- 0.11  5.32 +/- 0.11
           --------------------------------------
SAMPLE     * 237Np
            . Oxide form            NpO2
            . Diameter              8 cm
            . Half life             2.144E+06 y
            . Specific activity     26031+/-85 Bq/mg
            . Mass                  6.36+/-0.11 mg
            . Contaminations        241Am 1.6E-5 mg
            . Surface concentration 249+/-25 E+15 at/cm2
           * 238U
            . Oxide form            U3O8
            . Diameter              5.2 cm
            . Half life             4.468E+09 y
            . Specific activity     12.44+/-0.01 Bq/mg
            . Mass                  9.90+/-0.13 mg (front)
                                    9.03+/-0.12 mg (back)
            . Contaminations        -
            . Surface concentration 1112+/-95 E+15 at/cm2 (front)
                                    1120+/-100 E+15 at/cm2 (back)
           * 235U (to study influence of low energy neutrons)
            . Oxide form            U3O8
            . Diameter              5.2 cm
            . Half life             7.038E+08 y
            . Specific activity     79.98+/-0.06 Bq/mg
            . Mass                  4.96+/-0.06 mg
            . Contaminations        234U 9E-05 mg
            . Surface concentration 626+/-90 E+15 at/cm2
DETECTOR   (IOCH) MicroMegas detector
HISTORY    (20120629C) M.M.
           (20150810U) M.M. Ref. J,NDS,119,52,2014 added.
            Authors' names N.G.Nicolis, E.Berthoumieux added.
           (20240717A) On. Major revision in 002. 003 added.
           (20250629A) On+VD. Recompiled.
ENDBIB              56
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           59
SUBENT        23189002   20250629   20260826   20260826       2323
BIB                  8         26
REACTION  1((93-NP-237(N,F),,SIG)/(92-U-238(N,F),,SIG))
          2(93-NP-237(N,F),,SIG)
MONITOR   2(92-U-238(N,F),,SIG)
DECAY-DATA (93-NP-237,2.144E+6YR)
           (92-U-238,4.468E+9YR)
           (92-U-235,7.038E+8YR)
ANALYSIS   Influence of scattered neutrons was estimated by MCNP5
            and by blank measurement.
           Influence of low energy neutrons was estimated by
            237Np/235U measurement and by 74Ge(n,g)75mGe
           measurement with a HPGe detector.
CORRECTION Corrected for
            . subthreshold counts (5-7%)
            . detection efficiency
            . dead time (1.5% for 237Np, negligible for 238U)
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-S)         Statistical uncertainty      (<3%)
           (ERR-1,1.3,1.7) Target mass             (1.3-1.7%)
           (ERR-2,,0.5)    Subthreshold counts        (<0.5%)
           (ERR-3,2.,3.)   Detection efficiency        (2-3%)
           (ERR-4,3.,4.)   Neutron fluence             (3-4%)
          2(MONIT-ERR,,0.9) U-238 c-s uncertainty     (<0.9%)
STATUS    1(TABLE) Private communication with Maria Diakaki
          2(TABLE,,M.Diakaki,J,EPJ/A,49,62,2013) Table 3
HISTORY    (20240717A) On. EN-ERR -> EN-RSL-HW
           (20250625R) On. Np/U ratio received from Maria Diakaki.
           (20250629A) On+VD. Np/U ratio added.
ENDBIB              26
NOCOMMON             0          0
DATA                 7          4
